---
import type {RevisedCapability} from '../data/capabilityRedesign';
import {prototypeApproval} from '../data/capabilityRedesign';
import CapabilityPartFigure from './CapabilityPartFigure.astro';
import CapabilityReference from './CapabilityReference.astro';
import CapabilityEvidence from './CapabilityEvidence.astro';
import CapabilityInquiry from './CapabilityInquiry.astro';
import {libraryGuide} from '../data/resourceLibrary';
import '../styles/prototype-machining.css';
interface Props {page:RevisedCapability;quoteHref:string}
const {page,quoteHref}=Astro.props;
const cooling={...page.parts[1],text:'Intake and cooling interfaces for prototype fit checks. Define joints and any supplied-part scope.'};
const throttle={...page.parts[2],text:'Bores, mounting and actuator interfaces for development checks.'};
const materialLinks=[['Aluminum','aluminum-cnc-parts'],['Stainless steel','stainless-steel-cnc-parts'],['Copper & brass','copper-brass-cnc-parts'],['Engineering plastics','plastic-machined-parts']];
---
<div class="prototype-page">
 <section class="cx-intro" data-core-section="service"><header><h1>{page.plan.title}</h1><p class="cx-lead">Covers, housings and custom parts for fit, assembly and design evaluation. Machined to an agreed revision, with the checks needed for your next decision.</p></header><CapabilityPartFigure part={page.parts[0]} eager class="cx-intro-part"/><div class="cx-intro-actions"><a class="rd-button" href={quoteHref}>Prepare RFQ email</a><a class="rd-link" href="#part-examples">Define the evaluation</a><a class="cx-order-link" href="#order-conditions">Order & timing conditions</a></div></section>
 <section class="prototype-section prototype-scope" id="part-examples" data-core-section="evaluation-scope"><header><h2>Define what the prototype must answer</h2><p>State whether the review is for fit, assembly, appearance or a defined functional question. Mark fixed interfaces, mounting datums and clearances, including the cover fits to evaluate.</p></header><div class="prototype-references"><CapabilityReference part={cooling} namedLink singleEntry/><CapabilityReference part={throttle} namedLink singleEntry/></div><div class="prototype-application"><h3>Automotive &amp; motorcycle prototypes</h3><div><p>These component references do not establish a customer project, sector approval or vehicle performance. Agree pressure, functional or vehicle tests separately, including procedures, fixtures, limits and responsibility.</p></div></div></section>
 <section class="prototype-section prototype-approval" id="engineering-fit" data-core-section="approval-record"><header><h2>Keep the revision, checks and approval together</h2></header><table class="rd-table rd-stacked"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Stage</th><th scope="col">Input</th><th scope="col">Method & responsibility</th><th scope="col">Reviewable result</th></tr></thead><tbody>{prototypeApproval.map(row=><tr><th scope="row">{row.stage}</th><td data-label="Input">{row.input}</td><td data-label="Method & responsibility">{row.method}</td><td data-label="Reviewable result">{row.result}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table><div class="prototype-approval-evidence"><CapabilityEvidence id="cmm-room" caption="Original LZZ CMM photograph. Agree the measurement method, current calibration and report scope for the prototype; this is not its inspection result." sizes="180px"/><a class="rd-link" href={libraryGuide('machined-prototype-approval-checklist').href}>Prototype approval checklist</a></div></section>
 <section class="prototype-section prototype-differences" id="materials-finishes" data-core-section="production-differences"><header><h2>Record what differs from production</h2><p>Use the intended production material, condition and finish, or approve an alternative suited to this evaluation. Record which conclusions cannot carry over to the production part.</p></header><dl><div><dt>Material and condition</dt><dd>Record any change in alloy, temper, polymer grade, fillers or stock condition. Aluminum options include 6061 and 7075, subject to review of the temper, evaluation requirements and intended production specification. Confirm heat treatment and required material records.</dd></div><div><dt>Finish and working surfaces</dt><dd>Define the prototype finish and intended production treatment. Protect working fits, contact areas, threads and dimensions after treatment.</dd></div><div><dt>Edges and measurement state</dt><dd>Agree burr limits, edge quality, cleaning and measurement conditions. Identify application checks that the substitute material or finish cannot answer.</dd></div></dl><nav class="prototype-material-links" aria-label="Material selection">{materialLinks.map(([title,slug])=><a class="rd-link" href={'/capabilities/'+slug+'/'}>{title}</a>)}</nav><div class="prototype-next"><h3>The next revision or batch</h3><div><p>Record feedback, open issues and permitted changes. Identify and approve the next model / drawing revision before another prototype is machined. Keep acceptance tied to the tested revision and evaluation scope; agree the batch baseline, quantity, sampling and commercial order before repeat production.</p><nav aria-label="Next production steps"><a class="rd-link" href="/capabilities/low-volume-production/">Plan the first batch</a><a class="rd-link" href="/about/how-we-work/">Project responsibilities</a></nav></div></div></section>
 <CapabilityInquiry page={page} quoteHref={quoteHref} title="Request a prototype review" orderFirst coreSection="quotation"/>
</div>
